# QA replay of the desk's pictures across a price update (2026-10-26; the owner: "When finding prices in the stash it's
# important that they are recent", so the session prices the page again every five minutes while the desk is on screen,
# docs/DESIGN.md §3): the page is built again for new prices and for a reading, and must draw each cell's picture in its
# first frame, never blank until its file is decoded again (DeskBoard.ArtOf). "desk probe <n>" and "desk prices" say in
# their line how many pictures the frame before and the first frame after drew, of how many in the page's view. A
# developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it and what the lines must say: desk-prices.md beside
# this file. Times are in seconds.

tour end
map customs
wait 7

# The first reading; its cells come in and its totals count up, then the page stands.
desk 1
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-prices\before

# A reading that changed nothing: the page built again, nothing comes in.
desk probe 3
wait 2

# New prices, as the session's every five minutes bring them: the flea's a tenth up each time, the same reading.
desk prices
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk-prices\priced
desk prices
wait 2
desk prices
wait 2

# A reading that changed the backpack alone: it comes in, the rest is built again where it stands.
desk probe 2
wait 2
exit
